# Roster git verifies SSH commit signatures against, pointed at by
# gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile in .gitconfig. Format is:
#
#   <principal[,principal...]> <key-type> <key>
#
# The principal must match the commit's author email, so both addresses
# are listed: commits are authored as me@adrianlam.sh, but the GitHub
# noreply address shows up on anything committed through the web UI.
#
# The key is the public half of user.signingkey — the private half never
# leaves the 1Password agent.
